 "notes": "Kept all 7 old kinds (Saddle stirrup renamed Stirrup) and added Side saddle and Treeless saddle. Generic old model names became archetypes. Trimmed: English saddle keeps Ovation San Telmo, M. Toulouse Annice Jr and Premia Wide in m; Western: 55 models down to 30 versions plus 10 in m (repeat colourways or near-duplicates dropped: some Abetta, Fabtron, High Horse, Royal King, Tucker models); saddle pads 27 to 14 (Quarter sheet dropped: it is an exercise rug, not a pad); girths 24 to 16. McClellan placed under Western saddle as the American military archetype. Left out (no page retrieved or site blocked): Hermès Steinkraus/Allegro as separate versions (named only as predecessors), Devoucoux/CWD/Butet/Antares/Voltaire/Prestige/Albion model names (official sites redirected in loops or 403), Mayhew and Champion & Wilton side saddles, Barefoot treeless, Ogilvy pads, MDC and Freejump stirrups, Saumur saddlery tradition (no page describes it as a tradition). Brand stubs marked knowledge carry only facts I am confident of."
}